        "body": "Enabled video-analysis rules can trigger alarms for qualifying events such as line crossing, loitering, falls, unauthorized access, crowding, or unusual behavior. The alarm provides a record for operator investigation. Available detections, indicators, and response states depend on the deployed features and configuration.StageInformation or Action Live AlertFind the affected camera through indicators such as a red border, highlighting, flashing, or an alarm label. Notification RecordReview the alarm type, time, camera, location, severity, and status. Filter records using the available pending, severe, non-severe, or confirmed criteria. Associated FootageReview footage around the trigger to establish what happened, how long it lasted, and whether intervention is needed. A new alarm clip may still be processing. Alarm DetailsReview AI detections, adjust the event classification, update the status, and add notes. Confirm, close, or mark a false alarm using the actions available in the deployment. Status UpdatesUse the updated event record, notification display, and statistics to track follow-up work and review the response."
