        "id": "things-to-note",
        "heading": "Details and Actions",
        "body": "ContentHow to Review or Use It Event InformationCheck the type, timestamp, location, and camera name or ID. If the location and image disagree, investigate the camera association, installation location, and rule configuration. Associated ClipReview the sequence before, during, and after the trigger to establish the behavior, duration, and changes at the scene. Clip ProcessingA complete clip may not be available immediately. A clip might take approximately 15 seconds in one configuration; actual processing time depends on the deployment and clip interval. Check the displayed state and try again later. AI DetectionCompare the detection label with the footage when assessing a possible false alarm. Classification and StatusReclassify the event or apply the confirmation, response, closure, or false-alarm actions available to your role. State names follow the deployed interface. Notes and UpdatesRecord the findings, false-alarm cause, on-site action, and follow-up needed. After saving, check the notification and details for the latest result. TraceabilityUse the camera, footage, event information, and notes to reconstruct the event and the response."
