        "body": "SettingPurpose and Guidance Camera Selection and PreviewFind a camera by name, IP address, ID, location, or group. Use the live preview to identify the relevant entrance, corridor, or monitored area. Regions and Crossing LinesDraw the area where a rule applies or the boundary to monitor. Include the intended target area and exclude irrelevant backgrounds, reflections, and moving distractions. Detection AlgorithmsEnable the deployed capabilities needed for the task, such as geofencing, line crossing, people counting or tracking, face, mask, dwell-time, object, heatmap, motion, or crowd detection. Active ScheduleChoose days from Monday through Sunday and start and end times for working hours, after hours, duty periods, or other required intervals. DirectionWhere supported by the rule, detect entry, exit, or both. Align the direction with movement at the site. People-count ThresholdTrigger the relevant rule when the detected count reaches or exceeds the configured value, for crowding or occupancy-limit scenarios. VA Trigger DurationSet how long the condition must persist, for example 10 seconds. This is an example rather than a fixed value for every rule. A longer duration may filter brief disturbances; validate it against the monitoring objective. Multiple Rules and DeploymentConfigure multiple supported rules on one camera when needed. Deploy changes to the camera and verify the result. Add a DetectionOpen the add-detection dialog, enter a name and prompt, then save the item to the detection library. Enable it with the appropriate region, schedule, trigger interval, and parameters. Project-specific examples include smoking, sleeping, unusual lingering, or prohibited behavior; test the actual results before relying on them."
