    "id": "en-getting-started-checklist",
    "title": "Getting Started Checklist",
    "route": "/en/docs/getting-started",
    "category": "System Overview",
    "status": "Published",
    "owner": "Product Operations",
    "updatedAt": "2026-11-03",
    "version": "1.4",
    "readingTime": 2,
    "summary": "Before operational use, verify account access, live video, recordings, detection, and notification handling. Record failed checks and assign follow-up before relying on the workflow.",
    "tags": [
      "Getting Started",
      "Checklist",
      "English"
    ],
    "contentHtml": "<h2>Before You Begin</h2><p>Obtain an account from the administrator and confirm that the workstation can reach POLYTRON ONE. For the initial check, work with an administrator or delivery specialist to select a test camera, a recorded interval, a detection rule, and the required permissions.</p><p>Test detection only on approved devices, in an approved area, and under safe, controlled conditions. Coordinate the test to avoid disrupting monitoring or triggering an unnecessary site response.</p><h2>Acceptance Checklist</h2><ol><li><strong>Sign-in and permissions</strong>: Verify access to the menus, actions, and cameras required for the role.</li><li><strong>Live video</strong>: Open at least one authorized camera. Check that the feed plays, its displayed time is correct, and the device status is appropriate.</li><li><strong>Recordings</strong>: Select an interval known to contain footage. Verify that recording segments are shown and play correctly.</li><li><strong>AI detection</strong>: Under controlled conditions, perform an action that meets the test rule. Verify the detection and resulting alarm record.</li><li><strong>Notification response</strong>: Open the test alarm, review the clip, add a test note, and apply the agreed status action. Check that the list reflects the saved outcome.</li><li><strong>Record the outcome</strong>: Document passed checks and exceptions. Include camera IDs, test times, errors, and screenshots, and assign follow-up to the responsible person.</li></ol><h2>Initial Use Guidance</h2><p>At the start of a shift, review camera availability, system resources, and outstanding alarms on Home. Prepare the required Live View grids or tabs. If significant issues remain, follow the project’s acceptance and shift procedures to determine readiness for use.</p><p>Lock the workstation when stepping away and sign out when finished. Do not save credentials on shared devices.</p>",
