    "version": "1.4",
    "readingTime": 2,
    "summary": "Resolve common access, camera, recording, alarm, notification, and export issues. Use the answers below to identify the next check, then continue in the relevant module.",
    "tags": [
      "FAQ",
      "Support",
      "English"
    ],
    "contentHtml": "<h2>Accounts and Permissions</h2><h3>Why Are Some Pages or Cameras Missing After Sign-in?</h3><p>Check the assigned role’s feature permissions and camera permissions. Access to a page does not necessarily include access to the cameras needed for the task. Ask an administrator to verify the role’s scope.</p><h3>What If the Password-reset Email Does Not Arrive?</h3><p>Enter the email address linked to your account, check the spam folder, and use the latest verification code or link. If the message still does not arrive, ask an administrator to check the account email and mail service.</p><h2>Cameras and Live Video</h2><h3>Why Is There No Image When a Camera Is Online?</h3><p>Online status indicates basic connectivity. Verify the stream URL, codec, browser media support, and account permissions, then test the feed.</p><h3>Why Can Video Quality Decrease in a Multi-camera View?</h3><p>A multi-camera view may use a lower-bitrate substream to reduce bandwidth and client load. For detail, select a single view or an available higher-quality stream. The device and deployment determine supported modes.</p><h2>Recordings and Exports</h2><h3>Why Is No Recording Available in Playback?</h3><p>Verify the camera, date, time, and time zone. Check schedule coverage, storage, and recording-task execution. Current online status does not establish that footage exists for an earlier interval.</p><h3>What If an Exported Video Will Not Open?</h3><p>Verify that the download completed and check the file size. Try the project-recommended player. If the file still does not open, export a shorter interval and retain the error, footage interval, and camera ID.</p><h2>AI Alarms and Notifications</h2><h3>Why Is No Alarm Triggered Even Though Live Video Works?</h3><p>Check algorithm enablement, rule deployment, region, direction, threshold, duration, and active schedule. Test an approved, safe example that meets the rule.</p><h3>Why Is a Known Alarm Missing from Notifications?</h3><p>Check time and status filters, auto refresh, account visibility, and whether the event was closed or archived. Reading a notification or stopping an alert does not complete the response.</p><h3>How Should I Reduce Frequent False Alarms?</h3><p>Retain representative clips and document observable causes. Review region size, reflections, background motion, occlusion, thresholds, and active periods. Change one relevant condition at a time, then retest.</p><h2>Get Help</h2><p>Start with Troubleshooting. If the issue persists, send the administrator the page URL, time and time zone, camera ID, steps, expected and actual results, error text, screenshots, and relevant logs. Remove passwords, tokens, and complete credentials before sharing.</p>",
